(property "Description" "Commercial module, functional pad names from maker documentation. Factory regulator, level shifting, decoupling and bias resistors remain on module. | module | VIN from RP2040-Zero 3V3, not 5V: maker requires supply equal MCU logic level. Both PS0 and PS1 strapped high select SPI. INT and RST are connected, as required for stable SPI.; Never route BNO085 on Q6A I2C; full quaternion reports only, CRC frame forwarded by Pico. E5 owns external pack ESD.; The official Adafruit Eagle H_INTN pin is an output connected directly to INT pad. Earlier draft open_collector type was incorrect and is corrected from source, not suppressed for ERC.; PS1 straps high. PS0/WAKE is pulled high through 1k (overrides the module factory10k pulldown) and connected to Zero GP8: keep it high throughout reset and first INT, then pulse low to wake the BNO for host-initiated SPI as required by the CEVA datasheet." (at 0 0 0) (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)) (hide yes)))
